{"slug": "osso-buco", "nyt_id": 1807, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1807-osso-buco", "name": "Osso Buco", "author": "Mark Bittman", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 120, "raw": {"total": "2 hours"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 tablespoon olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "4 center-cut slices veal shank, 2 pounds or more", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "center-cut slices veal shank", "preparation": "2 pounds or more", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "3 or 4 cloves garlic, lightly mashed and peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "or 4 cloves garlic", "preparation": "lightly mashed and peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 anchovy fillets", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "anchovy fillets", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 cup dry white wine, chicken or beef stock, or water", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry white wine", "preparation": "chicken or beef stock, or water", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 teaspoons butter, optional", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "butter", "preparation": null, "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat a large, deep skillet over medium-high heat for a couple of minutes. Add the oil, swirl it around, and pour out any excess. Add the veal slices and cook until nicely browned on the first side, about 5 minutes. (For even browning, you can rotate the slices, but try not to disturb them too much.) Turn and brown the other side."}, {"position": 2, "text": "When the second side is just about completely browned, sprinkle with a little salt and pepper and add the garlic and anchovies to the pan. Cook, stirring a little, until the anchovies dissolve and the garlic browns, about 2 minutes. Add the liquid and let it bubble away for about a minute."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Turn the heat to low and cover the skillet. Five minutes later, check to see that the mixture is simmering — just a few bubbles appearing at once — and adjust the heat accordingly. Cook until the meat is very tender and pulling away from the bone, at least 90 minutes and probably somewhat more; turn the slices every half-hour or so. (When the meat is tender, you may turn off the heat and refrigerate the dish for up to 24 hours; reheat gently before proceeding.)"}, {"position": 4, "text": "Remove the meat to a warm platter and turn the heat to high. Boil the sauce until it becomes thick and glossy, about 5 minutes. Stir in the butter if you like, and serve the meat with the sauce spooned over it."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 449.1, "protein_g": 59.1, "carbohydrates_g": 3.1, "fat_g": 16.2, "saturated_fat_g": 4.9, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 233.5, "sodium_mg": 865.7, "fiber_g": 0.3, "sugar_g": 0.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 8.6, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["braise", "five ingredient", "garlic", "veal"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 327}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1998-12-30", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T03:51:59.061794+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "osso-buco-alla-milanese", "nyt_id": 3242, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/3242-osso-buco-alla-milanese", "name": "Osso Buco Alla Milanese", "author": "Florence Fabricant", "description": "Among hearty stew-like recipes, Italian osso buco ranks as a classic. Meaty veal shanks simmered with white wine and vegetables and served with risotto is to Milan what beef in red wine is to Burgandy. Osso buco means ''bone with a hole.'' The shank bone is hollow, filled with delectable marrow. It is traditional to serve long, slender marrow spoons with this dish to facilitate removing the marrow and enjoying it (cocktail forks are adequate substitutes). Gremolata, a garnish of minced lemon peel, garlic and parsley, is another requirement.", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 20, "cook_minutes": 120, "total_minutes": 140, "raw": {"total": "2 hours 20 minutes", "prep": "20 minutes", "cook": "2 hours"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "4 to 6 tablespoons olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": 6.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "6 portions of veal shank (about 6 pounds total), see Tip", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "portions of veal shank (about 6 pounds total)", "preparation": "see Tip", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¼ cup flour", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 cup finely chopped onions", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped onions", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "½ cup finely chopped carrots", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped carrots", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ cup finely chopped celery", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped celery", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 large garlic clove, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large garlic clove", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 ½ cups dry white wine", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry white wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 ½ cups peeled, seeded, chopped fresh tomatoes (canned Italian tomatoes, drained and chopped, may be substituted)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "peeled", "preparation": "seeded, chopped fresh tomatoes (canned Italian tomatoes, drained and chopped, may be substituted)", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 ¼ cups well-flavored veal, beef or chicken stock", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "well-flavored veal", "preparation": "beef or chicken stock", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "½ teaspoon dried thyme", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "dried thyme", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "Gremolata (see recipe)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "gremolata (see recipe)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Melt the oil in a heavy casserole large enough to hold the veal in a single layer. Dust shank pieces with flour and lightly brown on all sides over medium heat. You may find the browning easier if you do not put all the shanks in the pan at once. Do not allow them to become dark or blackened. Remove the shanks from the casserole and lower heat."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees."}, {"position": 3, "text": "To the casserole, add onions, carrots and celery and saute, stirring until they begin to soften. Add garlic and saute a minute longer. Add wine and cook over medium-high heat, scraping the pan until all the brown bits clinging to it have dissolved. Stir in the tomatoes, stock and thyme."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Return the shanks to the casserole, basting with the sauce. Season with salt and pepper, cover and bake in the preheated oven about 1 ½ hours, until the meat is tender when pierced with a fork. Baste the shanks several times during baking."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Remove shanks to a serving dish and keep warm. Taste sauce and season with salt and pepper if necessary. If the sauce is too thin (it should be about the consistency of cream), place the pan on top of the stove and boil down the sauce for several minutes."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Pour sauce over the shanks and top with a little of the gremolata. Pass the rest on the side."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 779.3, "protein_g": 98.6, "carbohydrates_g": 14.1, "fat_g": 29.5, "saturated_fat_g": 7.1, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 376.5, "sodium_mg": 1653.0, "fiber_g": 2.0, "sugar_g": 4.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 18.0, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": ["dairy-free"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["braise", "dry white wine", "one pot", "saute", "tomato", "veal"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2023/02/26/multimedia/FF-Osso-Bucco-bctk/FF-Osso-Bucco-bctk-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 688}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1985-10-27", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T05:03:30.304613+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "osso-buco-portobello", "nyt_id": 1012982, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1012982-osso-buco-portobello", "name": "Osso Buco Portobello", "author": "Florence Fabricant", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 105, "raw": {"total": "PT1H45M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 tablespoons flour", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "4 pieces veal shank, 2 inches thick", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "piece", "item": "veal shank", "preparation": "2 inches thick", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "4 large portobello mushrooms, stemmed, in slices ½ -inch wide", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "large portobello mushrooms", "preparation": "stemmed, in slices ½ -inch wide", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup finely chopped shallots", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped shallots", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "4 cloves garlic, sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 cup dry red wine", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry red wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "⅓ cup beef stock", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "unit": "cup", "item": "beef stock", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 tablespoons red wine vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "red wine vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "6 sprigs fresh thyme, more for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": "sprig", "item": "fresh thyme", "preparation": "more for garnish", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Season flour with salt and pepper. Spread on a plate and dust osso buco with it. In a 4- to 5-quart casserole, heat 3 tablespoons oil on medium high. Add meat and brown on both sides. Remove. Add mushrooms and cook, stirring, about 5 minutes, until they start to wilt and no longer look dry. Remove."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Add remaining tablespoon oil to pot, reduce heat to low and sauté shallots and garlic until just starting to brown. Deglaze with wine and stock. Season generously with pepper. Stir in vinegar. Return meat and mushrooms to pot, add thyme, cover and cook on very low about 1 hour 15 minutes, basting meat a few times, until meat is tender."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Season sauce with salt as needed. Transfer meat, mushrooms and sauce to a warm platter, garnish with thyme sprigs and serve."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 580.5, "protein_g": 62.1, "carbohydrates_g": 15.9, "fat_g": 24.6, "saturated_fat_g": 5.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 2.9, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 225.0, "sodium_mg": 1285.5, "fiber_g": 3.4, "sugar_g": 5.1, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-main-course"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["one-pot", "portobello", "veal"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/01/dining/osso-buco-portobello/osso-buco-portobello-superJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/01/dining/osso-buco-portobello/osso-buco-portobello-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 92}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-01-06", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:38:59Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "osso-buco-style-turkey-necks", "nyt_id": 1013591, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013591-osso-buco-style-turkey-necks", "name": "Osso Buco-Style Turkey Necks", "author": "Melissa Clark", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "3 to 4 servings", "min": 3, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 165, "raw": {"total": "PT2H45M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "3 pounds turkey necks, cut crosswise into thirds", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "lb", "item": "turkey necks", "preparation": "cut crosswise into thirds", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ¼ teaspoons coarse kosher salt", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "unit": "tsp", "item": "coarse kosher salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 ¼ teaspoons black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "unit": "tsp", "item": "black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "3 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 carrots, chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "carrots", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 celery stalk, chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "celery stalk", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 onion, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "onion", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "3 garlic cloves, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 tablespoon tomato paste", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "tomato paste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "⅔ cup dry white wine", "group": null, "quantity": 0.6666666666666666, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry white wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 cup chicken broth", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "chicken broth", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 large rosemary sprig", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large rosemary sprig", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "2 sage sprigs", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "sage sprigs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "2 thyme sprigs", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "thyme sprigs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "¼ cup finely chopped fresh parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped fresh parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "½ teaspoon finely grated lemon zest", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "finely grated lemon zest", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat the oven to 325 degrees. Season the necks with 1 teaspoon each salt and pepper."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Heat the oil in a large skillet or Dutch oven over medium-high heat. Cook the necks, turning occasionally, until dark golden, about 10 minutes, then transfer to a plate."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Add the carrots, celery, onion and 2 of the garlic cloves to the skillet. Cook until the vegetables are soft and golden, about 5 minutes. Season with ¼ teaspoon each salt and pepper. Stir in the tomato paste and cook until darkened, 1 to 2 minutes. Pour in the wine and simmer, scraping up any browned bits at the bottom of the skillet, 2 minutes. Add the broth, rosemary, sage and thyme (tie herbs together with kitchen twine if desired). Return necks to the pot. Bring liquid to a simmer. Cover pot and place in the oven. Cook, turning necks occasionally, until they are very tender, 1 ½ to 2 hours."}, {"position": 4, "text": "When the turkey necks are done, transfer to a serving platter. Bring the liquid in the pan to a boil over medium-high heat; simmer until thickened, 5 to 10 minutes. Pour the sauce over the necks. Combine the remaining garlic, parsley and lemon zest in a small bowl; sprinkle over the turkey."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 621.25, "protein_g": 59.5, "carbohydrates_g": 14.8, "fat_g": 32.2, "saturated_fat_g": 7.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 6.4, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 393.0, "sodium_mg": 1254.6, "fiber_g": 4.2, "sugar_g": 4.9, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-main-course"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": []}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 20}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2011-05-11", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:56:00Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "osso-buco-with-anchovies-and-sage", "nyt_id": 7099, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/7099-osso-buco-with-anchovies-and-sage", "name": "Osso Buco With Anchovies and Sage", "author": "Bryan Miller", "description": "Bryan Miller", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 180, "raw": {"total": "3 hours"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "Flour for dredging meat", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "flour for dredging meat", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "6 veal shanks or lamb shanks, about 1 ½ inches thick", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "veal shanks or lamb shanks", "preparation": "about 1 ½ inches thick", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ cup olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "8 cloves garlic, peeled and crushed", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "peeled and crushed", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 anchovy fillets", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "anchovy fillets", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "10 leaves fresh sage or 1 ½ teaspoons dried", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "leaves fresh sage or 1 ½ teaspoons dried", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 cups dry white wine", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry white wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Chicken stock as needed", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "chicken stock as needed", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 tablespoon butter", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "Salt and pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Dredge shanks in flour and shake off excess. Pour olive oil into a heavy-bottomed skillet over medium-high heat. When oil is hot, add shanks and brown on both sides. Remove meat from pan, and place in large ovenproof casserole."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Pour off all but 2 tablespoons of the oil in the pan. Add garlic, anchovies and sage, and saute for 2 minutes. Add white wine and bring to a boil, scraping bottom of the pan. Pour liquid over meat in casserole. Season with salt and pepper. Cover and bake for 2 ½ hours, or until meat is soft."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Remove meat to a serving platter. Pour juices in the casserole into a saucepan. There should be about 1 ½ cups; if not, add chicken stock. Reduce liquid by half: about 10 to 15 minutes over high heat. Swirl in the butter, seasoning to taste, and pour liquid over the meat. Serve with assorted root vegetables."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 1230.6, "protein_g": 89.1, "carbohydrates_g": 13.3, "fat_g": 83.0, "saturated_fat_g": 33.2, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 309.7, "sodium_mg": 1578.6, "fiber_g": 1.3, "sugar_g": 2.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 44.6, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["bake", "braise", "dry white wine", "sage", "saute", "veal", "winter"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 116}, "video_url": null,